         "My whisper server" on the chip, "Your saved whisper server" in the carry-over and
         "speech server" in two error strings — four names for one machine. "(optional)" was
         additionally false: once that provider is chosen this is the only address there is. -->
    <string name="field_server_url">Whisper server address</string>
    <string name="field_search">Search notes and transcripts</string>
    <string name="field_body_hint">Write, or use #tags inline</string>

    <!-- States the person reads while waiting or when there is nothing -->
    <!-- true because: TodayScreen.kt RecordButton — the button is disabled while `Transcribing` or `PreparingEngine`, and RecordStatus counts the seconds beside it. -->
    <string name="state_transcribing">Transcribing…</string>
    <!-- true because: VoiceViewModel.stopAndTranscribe — under MIN_SAMPLES the recording is not sent to an engine at all. -->
    <string name="state_nothing_heard">Nothing was heard.</string>
    <!-- REQ-052 / H11. true because: Recorder.silenced is AudioRecordingConfiguration
         .isClientSilenced() plus AudioManager.isMicrophoneMute(), checked per read loop, and
         VoiceViewModel maps it to VoiceState.Silenced while the recorder is still running.
         **It deliberately does not say "nothing heard":** Meta's *Horizon OS Audio* says the
         stream "isn't closed and is provided empty audio data", so the recording IS running and
         the headset is the one that stopped it hearing. Blaming the person for the system's
         decision is the copy defect this string exists to avoid. -->
    <string name="state_microphone_silenced">The headset has muted the microphone. The recording is still running and nothing is reaching it.</string>
    <!-- true because: VoiceViewModel.onPermissionResult — reached only after a refusal since DEC-0044, which is why it explains rather than instructs. -->
    <string name="state_needs_microphone">The microphone is needed to dictate.</string>
    <!-- T-031. Shown only after a refusal now: before the system dialog the reason is obvious
         from the button that was just pressed, and in a headset a rationale screen is one more
         thing to aim at. -->
    <string name="action_ask_again">Ask again</string>
    <!-- Same words as core-common's `action_write_note`, and deliberately a second string: that
         one is a banner action the mapper chooses, this one is a control this screen draws. A
         shared id would tie a copy change on one to the other. -->
    <!-- Four minutes of waiting must not end in an absence: `Done` used to become `Idle`, the
         progress bar vanished, and nothing said the bytes had arrived or been verified. -->
    <!-- true because: VoiceViewModel — emitted on DownloadProgress.Done, which fires only after the digest has been verified (DEC-0016). -->
    <string name="state_model_ready">The speech model is ready. Press Record.</string>
    <!-- DEC-0010 deleted the hold gesture; this sentence outlived it, and sat one screen
         away from `today_empty` saying "Press Record" — one build, two gestures. -->
    <!-- true because: PermissionRequester.openAppSettings returning false — the intent resolves to nothing on this device, so there is no page and reinstalling is the only route left (D-02). -->
    <string name="state_app_settings_unavailable">This headset has no page where a refused permission can be turned back on. Reinstalling the app is the only way to be asked again.</string>
    <!-- Two callers since B-090: the editor opened on a row that is no longer there, and a
         *Transcribe again* whose note was deleted while the decode ran. Re-reading the row before
         the write is what made the second one visible at all — the snapshot could not see it, and
         wrote the deleted note back.
         true because: NoteEditorScreen (note == null) and NotesViewModel.retranscribe, which
         returns Failed rather than resurrecting a row `undoDelete` alone may restore. -->
    <string name="state_note_gone">This note is gone.</string>
    <string name="state_nothing_written">Nothing written yet.</string>
    <!-- REQ-061: "Space" is this product's name for the immersive surface (`CONTEXT.md`), and
